4. Assess demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return rate for the anomaly month vs the 24-month average return rate for that region×product, (b) whether the following 1-3 months show a sales drop (reversal), (c) the magnitude of the spike relative to the 24-month std. Save a structured assessment table to offline_data/stuffing_signals.csv → code_agent
